        "original_id": "aea0189e-2701-591a-9c22-a7f7822606c6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: True Williams, Mark Twain, Bill Nye, George W. Peck, Joaquin Miller\n- Works: The Adventures of Tom Sawyer\n- Roles: American artist, illustrator, writer\n- Topics: book illustration, novels\n\nFacts:\n- True Williams was born on March 22, 1839, and died on November 23, 1897.\n- True Williams was an American artist known as the most prolific illustrator of Mark Twain's books and novels.\n- True Williams also illustrated works by writers Bill Nye, George W. Peck, Joaquin Miller, and others while working with a number of publishers.\n- The Adventures of Tom Sawyer is an 1876 novel by Mark Twain.\n- The Adventures of Tom Sawyer is about a young boy growing up along the Mississippi River.",
